Add voice macros: spoken phrase expands to a saved snippet

Port the macOS voice-macro feature end to end:

- Core: VoiceMacro model + pure VoiceMacroMatcher (lowercase, strip
  punctuation, trim; whole-transcript exact match, first match wins).
- Pipeline: when a macro matches the raw transcript (non-command intents),
  paste its payload verbatim and bypass transcription cleanup (status "macro").
- Settings: VoiceMacros persist as part of DictationSettings; a new "Voice
  macros" editor adds/edits/removes command/expansion pairs.
- Tests: L0 matcher cases, L3 pipeline macro test, L1 settings round-trip.

Inner loop GREEN at 197 (was 186); app builds x86 clean.

